(7706666, 1265906, 30861, '<td valign="top">Flawless. 10 from me. I don''t expect it will get a lot of love, but it''s beautifully composed and processed.</td>', 'Flawless. 10 from me. I don''t expect it will get a lot of love, but it''s beautifully composed and processed.', '2021-11-15 00:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706745, 1265689, 100831, '<td valign="top">Reflections are fun. These are nicely balanced.</td>', 'Reflections are fun. These are nicely balanced.', '2021-11-15 14:22:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706746, 1265914, 100831, '<td valign="top">This definitely warrants a song or two! Nicely done.</td>', 'This definitely warrants a song or two! Nicely done.', '2021-11-15 14:23:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706795, 1265892, 15511, '<td valign="top">"Two reinforced concrete speaker towers are east and west of the stadia of the bathhouse. Both towers are 35 feet high. The simple concrete pier of each tower artfully flanges out toward the speaker housing at the top. The housing is circular in plan, and has a series of concentric horizontal bands shielding the opening for the speaker. A metal ladder bolted to the concrete base provides access to the speaker housing. The towers are of the same Streamlined-Moderne design of the other WPA structures."

<br/>
<br/><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20080226162331///www.nps.gov/history/history/online_books/harrison/harrison29.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Aquatic Park History</a></td>', '"Two reinforced concrete speaker towers are east and west of the stadia of the bathhouse. Both towers are 35 feet high. The simple concrete pier of each tower artfully flanges out toward the speaker housing at the top. The housing is circular in plan, and has a series of concentric horizontal bands shielding the opening for the speaker. A metal ladder bolted to the concrete base provides access to the speaker housing. The towers are of the same Streamlined-Moderne design of the other WPA structures."


Aquatic Park History', '2021-11-16 00:44:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7707123, 1265910, 38162, '<td valign="top">Great subject and capture but lighting isn''t there enough to make it all pop.  GL.</td>', 'Great subject and capture but lighting isn''t there enough to make it all pop.  GL.', '2021-11-19 15:31:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7707124, 1265725, 38162, '<td valign="top">Looks like we have our winner!  10. Gl.</td>', 'Looks like we have our winner!  10. Gl.', '2021-11-19 15:35:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7707126, 1265848, 38162, '<td valign="top">Really like your choice of subject here - just not the edit - would like to see more pop from contrast and structure. This one begs for some drama.</td>', 'Really like your choice of subject here - just not the edit - would like to see more pop from contrast and structure. This one begs for some drama.', '2021-11-19 15:42:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(7707304, 1265725, 30214, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Larry, great find! The good thing about my Olympus is that in such cases I can put it on the floor instead of laying down myself )). It has a flip-out back screen that I can use to compose the shot. And it allows me to use a long exposure to lower my ISO.</td>', 'Congratulations Larry, great find! The good thing about my Olympus is that in such cases I can put it on the floor instead of laying down myself )). It has a flip-out back screen that I can use to compose the shot. And it allows me to use a long exposure to lower my ISO.', '2021-11-22 07:49:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707307, 1265725, 103142, '<td valign="top">This is so gorgeous. The tones are magnificent!</td>', 'This is so gorgeous. The tones are magnificent!', '2021-11-22 08:29:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707308, 1265905, 103142, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot - great find!</td>', 'Very cool shot - great find!', '2021-11-22 08:29:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707309, 1265853, 103142, '<td valign="top">I like the colors - I dont know about aurora hdr! Ill have to look it up! Congrats!!</td>', 'I like the colors - I dont know about aurora hdr! Ill have to look it up! Congrats!!', '2021-11-22 08:30:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707310, 1265689, 103142, '<td valign="top">Great fun! Congrats!!</td>', 'Great fun! Congrats!!', '2021-11-22 08:31:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707325, 1265853, 30982, '<td valign="top">The colors on this are just wonderful!  Do I have to go get a Galaxy S21 now?  :-)  Lovely shot, and processed perfectly, as always!</td>', 'The colors on this are just wonderful!  Do I have to go get a Galaxy S21 now?  :-)  Lovely shot, and processed perfectly, as always!', '2021-11-22 11:09:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707344, 1265914, 56502, '<td valign="top">Nice! Where is that?</td>', 'Nice! Where is that?', '2021-11-22 15:41:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7707368, 1265725, 3306, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations Larry, great find! The good thing about my Olympus is that in such cases I can put it on the floor instead of laying down myself )). It has a flip-out back screen that I can use to compose the shot. And it allows me to use a long exposure to lower my ISO. </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>Thanks for the comment Lev,

<br/>  My camera Also has the flip screen. I had to place my camera in  a very tight corner which did not allow me to use the screen. It was so dark I couldn''t see the screen anyway so I had to stabilize the camera while resting it on the ground and moving the camera as I layed on the ground to take the shot manually. I basically took several blind shots hoping I would get the angle I wanted.  In hindsight there were other things I could have tried like a bean bag to stabilize the camera and a bluetooth connection to my cellphone to see the shot I was taking. Next time!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-11-23 11:16:55.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Congratulations Larry, great find! The good thing about my Olympus is that in such cases I can put it on the floor instead of laying down myself )). It has a flip-out back screen that I can use to compose the shot. And it allows me to use a long exposure to lower my ISO. 

Thanks for the comment Lev,

  My camera Also has the flip screen. I had to place my camera in  a very tight corner which did not allow me to use the screen. It was so dark I couldn''t see the screen anyway so I had to stabilize the camera while resting it on the ground and moving the camera as I layed on the ground to take the shot manually. I basically took several blind shots hoping I would get the angle I wanted.  In hindsight there were other things I could have tried like a bean bag to stabilize the camera and a bluetooth connection to my cellphone to see the shot I was taking. Next time!', '2021-11-23 11:15:10.000000', '2021-11-23 11:16:55.000000', 0),
